Report #166 (shaman Elemental: Chain Lightning "doesn't work at all,
unusable"): two stacked causes, both fixed.

1. Data: the DBC's ChainTarget field is 0 on ranks 49238/49239/49240
   (the per-level ranks between rank 1's 421 [3] and the WotLK-end
   49271 [3]). Spell::SelectImplicitChainTargets reads that field and
   skips chain selection entirely when maxTargets <= 1, so the spell hit
   exactly one target for anyone who learned those ranks. Fixed by
   rev_chain_lightning_chaintarget.sql (pending_db_world) restoring
   EffectChainTargets_2 = 3.

2. Core: SPELLVALUE_MAX_TARGETS was honored only by
   SelectImplicitAreaTargets, so the module's Elemental-perk raise
   (SetSpellValue(SPELLVALUE_MAX_TARGETS, 99) in
   ApplyShamanElementalChainLightningTargets, ClassPerks.cpp:2508) was
   silently ignored for chain spells. SelectImplicitChainTargets now
   lets an explicit spell value win over the DBC ChainTarget, keeping
   SPELLMOD_JUMP_TARGETS as the fallback when no value is set.

Both halves are needed: the migration fixes every shaman (and any other
class whose learned chain ranks carry the broken 0), the core change
makes the perk's 99-target reach actually take effect.
